KONOHAGAKURE — HYUGA CLAN MAIN HOUSE POLICY

The Hyuga are the wielders of the Byakugan, a prized kekkei genkai of the Hidden Leaf. The clan is divided into the Main House (Soke) and the Branch House (Bunke).

Main House provisions:
- The Main House carries the clan's direct line of succession and its heir.
- The clan head bears responsibility for protecting the Byakugan secret and directing the Branch House.
- Marriage and succession within the Main House are managed to preserve the bloodline.
- The Main House is charged with the welfare and command of the Branch House, a duty it is expected to exercise honorably.

This policy is to be read alongside the Branch House Seal Policy. Clan disputes are settled by the clan head with Council oversight where they affect village security.
Maintained by the Hyuga clan head and the Administration Building.
